INTEREST TABLE
==============

Purpose
-------
Stores the approved interest tags that users and meetings can select from.

Fields
------
- Id: Generated integer primary key
- Name: One interest label (data type TBD)

TypeScript app model
--------------------
- A User and a Meeting can each have an Interest[]; each item is an Interest with an Id and Name.
- This describes the relationship in the application model, not how it is stored in the database.

Relationships
-------------
- A user can select multiple interests; an interest can be selected by multiple users.
- A meeting can have multiple interest tags; an interest can be used by multiple meetings.

Connections
-----------
- UserInterest connects a User.Id to an Interest.Id.
- MeetingInterest connects a Meeting.Id to an Interest.Id.
- A User.Id and Interest.Id pair can appear only once in UserInterest.
- A Meeting.Id and Interest.Id pair can appear only once in MeetingInterest.
- PostgreSQL needs a way to persist these many-to-many connections; an ORM may manage the join tables.
- The ORM has not been selected yet.

List management
---------------
- The list is curated.
- Users may suggest additions; how suggestions are reviewed is TBD.
